    claude-haiku-5-5-high+claude-fable-5-1/truth-04  23/24  =  95.8% [79.8, 99.3]
    claude-haiku-5-5-high+claude-fable-5-1/truth-05  23/24  =  95.8% [79.8, 99.3]

  Agreement is NOT accuracy: two labelers sharing a training
  distribution and a tool will be wrong together. What converts this
  into accuracy is a hand-labelled slice scored with pf_grade_verdicts().

the 60 overlap cases, by which models actually produced the two rows: 
           models     n agree   rate    usable
           <char> <int> <int> <char>    <char>
1: pass2-vs-pass2    36    33    92%       yes
2: pass1-vs-pass2    13    12    92% no (n<20)
3: pass1-vs-pass1    11    11   100% no (n<20)

Each subset is a different question. pass2-vs-pass2 is two runs of ONE 
procedure (fable twice, once as shard 1 and once as an escalation), which 
is run-to-run stability. Anything involving pass1 is cross-model. Neither 
is accuracy. 
 
